+{"body":"## Summary\n- Replace cached YouTube playlists with the latest YouTube API response during refresh instead of merging stale entries\n- Re-render the upload playlist selector after startup refresh resolves so visible UI does not keep stale localStorage markup\n- Keep newly created playlists saved additively through the existing create flow\n- Apply the related PR #185 late-helper lookup pattern to pipeline playlist refresh/create actions\n- Add case-study data and analysis under `docs/case-studies/issue-181`\n- Add Cypress coverage for upload and pipeline startup refresh replacing stale cached playlists with API results\n\nFixes Jhon-Crow/audio-recorder-with-visualization#181\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Sign in with YouTube playlist scope so `audio-recorder-youtube-token-state` is restored after restart.\n2. Store a stale playlist in `audio-recorder-youtube-playlists`.\n3. Restart/open the app while YouTube returns a different current playlist from `playlists.list?mine=true`.\n4. Before this fix, rendered playlist selectors could still show stale cached entries. After this fix, a successful refresh replaces the cache and re-renders selectors from the refreshed list.\n\n## Testing\n- `npm test -- --runInBand tests/YouTubeUploader.test.ts`\n- `npm run typecheck`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `npx cypress run --spec cypress/e2e/youtube-upload-ui.cy.js` passed the new startup playlist refresh regression; full spec still has 5 unrelated existing settings-sidebar failures where `#presetSettingsBtn` inherits `pointer-events: none`.\n- `npx cypress run --spec cypress/e2e/pipeline-mode.cy.js` passed the new pipeline stale-cache regression; full spec still has 2 unrelated existing failures in stage navigator active state and relative publish date update.\n\n## Case Study\nSee `docs/case-studies/issue-181/analysis.md` and collected raw artifacts in `docs/case-studies/issue-181/logs/`.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOQyCEds8AAAABHpVLdQ","author":{"login":"konard"},"authorAssociatio